author: codex
estimated_minutes: 20
acceptance_criteria: "A red source-contract regression rejects the best-effort empty-map claim; The comment distinguishes null-status rejection from ordinary nonzero rejection; The comment states parse and incomplete envelopes fail closed; Existing whole-tracker failure regressions remain green; npm run release:check passes exact 100/100/100/100"
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: Read the comment immediately before assertPmOutputFit in loadAppliedByTransaction and compare it with the following r.status nonzero CommandError branch.
resolution: "Replace the obsolete best-effort empty-map statement with the actual fail-closed pipeline: assertPmOutputFit rejects unusable null status, the following branch rejects ordinary nonzero command failures, and parse or completeness failures also refuse resume."
expected_result: "The comment states null-status output is rejected by assertPmOutputFit, ordinary nonzero results are rejected by the following branch, and parse/incomplete envelopes also fail closed."
actual_result: "The safety comment now matches the existing CommandError branches, and the source-contract test prevents the data-duplicating empty-map claim from returning."
